Ishida, and S. Sakaguchi. <year>2002</year>. Stimulation of CD25(+)CD4(+) regulatory T cells through GITR breaks immunological self-tolerance. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>135</fpage>&#x02013;142.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11812990</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Turk, M.J., J.D. Wolchok, J.A. Guevara-Patino, S.M. Goldberg, and A.N. Houghton. <year>2002</year>. Multiple pathways to tumor immunity and concomitant autoimmunity. <source>Immunol. Rev.</source> <volume>188</volume>:<fpage>122</fpage>&#x02013;135.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12445286</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sutmuller, R.P., L.M. van Duivenvoorde, A. van Elsas, T.N. Schumacher, M.E. Wildenberg, J.P. Allison, R.E. Toes, R. Offringa, and C.J. Melief. <year>2001</year>. Synergism of cytotoxic T lymphocyte-associated antigen 4 blockade and depletion of CD25<sup>+</sup> regulatory T cells in antitumor therapy reveals alternative pathways for suppression of autoreactive cytotoxic T lymphocyte responses. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>194</volume>:<fpage>823</fpage>&#x02013;832.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11560997</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Shimizu, J., S. Yamazaki, and S. Sakaguchi. <year>1999</year>. Induction of tumor immunity by removing CD25+CD4+ T cells: a common basis between tumor immunity and autoimmunity. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>163</volume>:<fpage>5211</fpage>&#x02013;5218.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10553041</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Groux, H., A. O'Garra, M. Bigler, M. Rouleau, S. Antonenko, J.E. de Vries, and M.G. Roncarolo. <year>1997</year>. A CD4+ T-cell subset inhibits antigen-specific T-cell responses and prevents colitis. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>389</volume>:<fpage>737</fpage>&#x02013;742.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9338786</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Terabe, M., S. Matsui, N. Noben-Trauth, H. Chen, C. Watson, D.D. Donaldson, D.P. Carbone, W.E. Paul, and J.A. Berzofsky. <year>2000</year>. NKT cell-mediated repression of tumor immunosurveillance by IL-13 and the IL-4R-STAT6 pathway. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>515</fpage>&#x02013;520.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11101874</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Moodycliffe, A.M., D. Nghiem, G. Clydesdale, and S.E. Ullrich. <year>2000</year>. Immune suppression and skin cancer development: regulation by NKT cells. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>521</fpage>&#x02013;525.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11101875</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sonoda, K.H., and J. Stein-Streilein. <year>2002</year>. Ocular immune privilege and CD1d-reactive natural killer T cells. <source>Cornea.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>S33</fpage>&#x02013;S38.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11995808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gorelik, E. <year>1983</year>. Concomitant tumor immunity and the resistance to a second tumor challenge. <source>Adv. Cancer Res.</source> <volume>39</volume>:<fpage>71</fpage>&#x02013;120.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6194674</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sonoda, K.H., M. Exley, S. Snapper, S.P. Balk, and J. Stein-Streilein. <year>1999</year>. CD1-reactive natural killer T cells are required for development of systemic tolerance through an immune-privileged site. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>190</volume>:<fpage>1215</fpage>&#x02013;1226.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10544194</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="jour